with the look of the code, you can shorten it (as example)
JavaScript:
const writenumber = v => {
  if (v < 1e3) return v; //999
  if (v >= 1e3 && v < 1e6) return +(v / 1e3).toFixed(2) + " thousand";
  if (v >= 1e6 && v < 1e9) return +(v / 1e6).toFixed(2) + " million";
  if (v >= 1e9 && v < 1e12) return +(v / 1e9).toFixed(2) + " billion";
  if (v >= 1e12) return +(v / 1e12).toFixed(2) + " trillion";
  //etc
};
you can go all the way down if needed (just as reference of another way)
even though, I use a different method for the currency, but it can have
its uses, not exactly sure where to use such big numbers though =)

